# Enhanced version

One of the most memorable long walks I’ve ever had was when I visited Saigon Zoo and Botanical Gardens. If I remember correctly, it was about two years ago when I was doing an internship at a local startup company.

At that time, my colleagues and I decided to spend a day at the zoo to relax and bond after a stressful period at work. Since the zoo is located in District 1 of Ho Chi Minh City, it was quite easy to get there. I chose to ride my motorbike because it was more convenient, and it only took me around 20 minutes.

We met at the entrance early in the morning and started walking around the zoo together. The place is quite huge, with many different areas for animals such as elephants, tigers, reptiles, birds, and many other species. We spent hours exploring different sections and watching the animals, and honestly, we became so absorbed in the experience that we completely lost track of time.

One moment I remember clearly was when we stayed at the elephant enclosure for quite a long time because the elephants looked so intelligent and gentle. By noon, my legs were already sore from walking so much, but I barely noticed because I was enjoying myself so much.

What made the experience even more special was the chance to spend quality time with my colleagues. We chatted, laughed a lot, and took many photos together to keep as memories. Although we don’t meet very often nowadays because everyone is busy with their own work and personal goals, I still consider that trip one of the most unforgettable experiences I’ve had.
